<title>GERMANY: Welteke confident EMU stability pact to work.</title>
<headline>Welteke confident EMU stability pact to work.</headline>
<dateline>KIEL, Germany 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Monday he was confident the planned stability pact for European Monetary Union (EMU) would work.</p>
<p>The stability pact is designed to ensure nations do not step outside agreed economic performance measures once inside European monetary union.</p>
<p>Kiel was speaking at a conference on EMU in the northern German city of Kiel.</p>
<p>--Franmkfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
